<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch company results week of Feb 10.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch company results week of Feb 10.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of Dutch company results for week beginning Monday Feb 10:</p>
<p>DATE--COMPANY----PERIOD--PROFIT------CONSENSUS----RANGE----PVS</p>
<p> 11/2  Unilever   Q4 96   net pft	 1043     869-1148   690</p>
<p> 11/2  Unilever   YR 96   net pft	 4094    3870-4210  3725</p>
<p> 12/2  KNP BT     Q4 96   net pft	   77	54-99     143</p>
<p> 12/2  KNP BT     YR 96   net pft	  187     167-210    510</p>
<p> 12/2  PolyGram   YR 96   net pft	  726     715-738    741</p>
<p> 13/2  RD/Shell   Q4 96   net pft	 1255    1029-1445   768</p>
<p> 13/2  RD/Shell   YR 96   net pft	 5508    5284-5700  4375</p>
<p> 13/2  RD/Shell   Q4 96   net pft CCS   1193    1005-1337   851</p>
<p> 13/2  RD/Shell   YR 96   net pft CCS   5108    5200-4844  4516</p>
<p> 13/2  Philips    Q4 96   net ord ops    526     387-750   1018</p>
<p> 13/2  Philips    YR 96   net ord ops   1331    1092-1525  2684</p>
<p>NOTES - Profit figures exclude extraordinary items and are in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell estimates are in millions of sterling and refer to historic cost net profit and current cost net profit excluding special items.</p>
<p>Unilever estimates are in guilders and include exceptional items. KNP BT estimates refer to net profit after deduction of dividend on preference shares.</p>
<p>Philips and PolyGram estimates refer to net profits from normal operations.</p>
<p>The following securities houses contributed to this survey: Amstgeld, Bangert Pontier, Delta Lloyd Bank, Generale Bank, ING, Kempen &amp; Co, MeesPierson, Rabo/IRIS, Wesselius.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31-20-504-5000 (Fax 31-20-504-5040)</p>
